in that it's a set of tools

00:02:48.920 --> 00:02:50.690
specifically for making
it easier and more

00:02:50.690 --> 00:02:53.607
affordable to run small
Kubernetes clusters, basically

00:02:53.607 --> 00:02:55.940
up to four nodes-- or less
than four nodes, if you want.

00:02:55.940 --> 00:02:58.130
So if you're trying to set up
a small developer environment,

00:02:58.130 --> 00:03:00.230
we actually have some
documentation and a developer

00:03:00.230 --> 00:03:02.420
template set up as well as
a new open-source utility

00:03:02.420 --> 00:03:04.914
called kubehost to get around
some of the cost things

00:03:04.914 --> 00:03:06.080
that happen with Kubernetes.

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:07.700
It can be a little bit
more expensive if you

00:03:07.700 --> 00:03:08.783
want to run a big cluster.

00:03:08.783 --> 00:03:10.160
So this is just
some nice tooling

00:03:10.160 --> 00:03:12.196
to get you started in
a nice, low-cost way.

00:03:12.196 --> 00:03:13.820
